# Duplicati on Railway
# The deploy form is zero-field except for the generated login password
# (see DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_PASSWORD below — Railway generates it).
# Copy this file to .env only if you run the wrapper outside Railway.

# Injected by Railway automatically — do not set these yourself:
# PORT — mapped by entrypoint.sh to DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_PORT.
# RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN — the public URL of this deployment.

# Consumed by the wrapper / template (the deploy form's only field):
# DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_PASSWORD=${{secret(32)}} — web UI login password.
#   Generated at deploy time. Find the generated value in the service
#   variables after deploy and sign in with it. Duplicati has no sign-up
#   form and no email step; without this variable first launch generates
#   a random password nobody can know.

# Baked into the Dockerfile as ENV (override in service variables if needed):
# DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_ALLOWED_HOSTNAMES=* — Duplicati rejects
#   hostname-based origins by default, which would block the Railway
#   public domain. Set it to your exact domain(s), semicolon-separated,
#   to lock this down.

# Consumed by entrypoint.sh (baked defaults; override only if you know why):
# DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_PORT — set from PORT by the wrapper; do not set directly.
# DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_INTERFACE=any — official image Docker default.
# DUPLICATI__SERVER_DATAFOLDER=/data — server database on the volume.
# DUPLICATI__DISABLE_DB_ENCRYPTION=true — official image Docker default
#   (avoids deriving the settings-DB key from the machine serial number,
#   which changes when a container moves). To encrypt the settings DB,
#   set this to false and set SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY (min 8 chars,
#   alphanumeric) — the key must be kept, or the database is unrecoverable.

# Upstream Duplicati variables that also apply (see README Configuration):
# DUPLICATI__WEBSERVICE_ALLOWED_HOSTNAMES — see above.
# SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY — only effective with DUPLICATI__DISABLE_DB_ENCRYPTION=false.
# TZ — container timezone for schedule evaluation (default UTC).
